From d7e2377dcf9c4e6d690872e55db9e6138028a362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:23:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: name the electricity resistance in the
 resist-electricity note

The borg_defend_aux_resist_e() acting pass notes "# Attempting to cast
RAcid", a copy of the acid routine's text one function above, so the
log names the wrong resistance every time the borg prepares its
electricity defence. The sibling routines name their own element
(RFire, RCold, RAcid, RPois).

Measured natively (native-c/resielec-174): a Warrior with a Ring of
Lightning next to an awake energy hound writes "# Attempting to cast
RAcid" on the original and "# Attempting to cast RElec" with the
correction, with identical queued keys; the plain-melee control, where
the routine finds no improvement and writes no note, is byte-identical.
Investigates diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#174.
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
index 05e6ac00e..1bb1c6a11 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
@@ -860,7 +860,7 @@ static int borg_defend_aux_resist_e(int p1)
         if (borg_simulate)
             return (p1 - p2);
 
-        borg_note("# Attempting to cast RAcid");
+        borg_note("# Attempting to cast RElec");
 
         /* do it! */
         if (borg_spell(RESISTANCE)) {
-- 
2.53.0

